{
 "section_summary": "This section consists chiefly of English summaries and translations of Japanese shortwave broadcasts from June and July 1941, enclosed with two FBI letters to the State Department. The broadcasts promote the Konoye cabinet’s policy, describe Japan’s move into French Indochina and the resulting asset freezes, and report on the wars in China, Europe, and the Soviet Union. Several program transcripts appear twice.",
